    "summary": "In Pakistan's Swat Valley, Malala Yousafzai defied Taliban extremism to advocate for female education. Surviving an assassination attempt, she became the youngest Nobel Peace Prize laureate and a champion for universal literacy.",
    "coverImage": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80",
